[Music]  this november dr mehmet oz famously  known for his long-running namesake tv  show will run as a trump-backed  republican candidate in pennsylvania's  senate race against democrat john  fetterman  naturally money is always a factor in  american political campaigns and dr oz  certainly acquired a fortune from his tv  days  according to a government financial  disclosure he made 9.3 million dollars  in pre-tax earnings last year alone  he also brought in just under 1 million  dollars last year for speeches and  appearances  and he has made royalties for a medical  device he patented with colleagues at  columbia university where he was a  professor of surgery  but much of oz's wealth and ties to  pennsylvania come from a different  source his wife's family  lisa oz's grandfather co-founded asplund  tree expert with his two brothers back  in 1928  asplund is now the 98th biggest private  company in america and the fifth largest  in pennsylvania  with over 33 000 employees and 4.7  billion dollars in revenue  the company trims trees for electric  utilities and municipalities and is run  by the third generation of asplunds and  owned by nearly 200 family members who  are collectively worth at least three  billion dollars  this probably helps explain why the  celebrity doctor was able to fund his  campaign with 12.1 million dollars of  personal loans and another 1.7 million  dollars in contributions  a spokesperson for asplan tree expert  told forbes the company is quote not in  any way involved in or invested in dr  oz's campaign or any other political  campaign  but did add quote individuals within the  organization may support political  parties or candidates  according to federal election commission  records at least 18 members of the  asplin clan contributed a total of 62  200 to dr oz's senate campaign on behalf  of themselves and their spouses  [Music]

